 ## Overview
-Transformers compute pairwise attention over input tokens to capture long-range dependencies that convolutions miss [S1, unofficial]. The Vision Transformer (ViT) adapts this architecture for images by treating fixed-size patches as tokens [S1, unofficial]. Builds on [Transformer-based Architectures](13148-transformer-based-architectures.md). In volume rendering, they are used for super-resolution and denoising, where their ability to attend across the full spatial extent of a subvolume helps recover large-scale structures that local convolutions miss [S1, unofficial].
